Authorization Form for","x":935,"y":664,"w":561,"h":43},{"text":"Change in Signers of Rebuttal Arguments","x":704,"y":720,"w":1018,"h":57},{"text":"Pursuant to California Elections Code SS9167, 9317 and 9504, the author(s) of the primary","x":252,"y":825,"w":1765,"h":58},{"text":"argument in favor of or against a measure may authorize in writing any other person or persons to","x":251,"y":903,"w":1906,"h":56},{"text":"sign the rebuttal argument.","x":250,"y":978,"w":524,"h":47},{"text":"The undersigned author(s) of the primary argument hereby authorize(s) the following","x":248,"y":1134,"w":1779,"h":55},{"text":"individual(s) to sign (up to five) the rebuttal argument to the primary argument in favor","x":249,"y":1208,"w":1809,"h":55},{"text":"of/against (circle one) Measure H","x":248,"y":1286,"w":706,"h":47},{"text":"for the Election to be held on November 3, 2026","x":1123,"y":1292,"w":989,"h":41},{"text":"(date of election)","x":1823,"y":1346,"w":266,"h":40},{"text":"NEW SIGNER(S) (PRINT CLEARLY):","x":248,"y":1431,"w":753,"h":49},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":249,"y":1556,"w":698,"h":46},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":248,"y":1702,"w":699,"h":47},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":248,"y":1848,"w":698,"h":48},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":248,"y":1995,"w":698,"h":47},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":248,"y":2140,"w":698,"h":47},{"text":"Thomas Morgan","x":994,"y":1548,"w":321,"h":44},{"text":"Charles Hoelter","x":995,"y":1694,"w":307,"h":36},{"text":"James Cravalho","x":994,"y":1841,"w":318,"h":37},{"text":"Arnout ter Schure","x":992,"y":1989,"w":346,"h":35},{"text":"Thomas Weissmiller","x":993,"y":2135,"w":399,"h":37},{"text":"(The new signers listed here must sign the Ballot Measure Rebuttal Argument Submission","x":247,"y":2265,"w":1887,"h":53},{"text":"Form)","x":246,"y":2316,"w":122,"h":45},{"text":"NAME(S) & SIGN","x":247,"y":2419,"w":346,"h":45},{"text":"Taso Zografos","x":253,"y":2507,"w":282,"h":45},{"text":"Printed Name and","x":247,"y":2574,"w":349,"h":36},{"text":"Printed Name and Signature of Author","x":248,"y":2726,"w":750,"h":48},{"text":"August 18, 2026","x":1711,"y":2518,"w":318,"h":44},{"text":"Date","x":1883,"y":2585,"w":89,"h":33},{"text":"Date","x":1884,"y":2738,"w":88,"h":35},{"text":"40 Tower Road, San Mateo, CA 94402","x":863,"y":2826,"w":686,"h":40},{"text":"P 650.312.5222 F 650.312.5348 email registrar@smcacre.gov web www.smcacre.gov","x":412,"y":2872,"w":1582,"h":50}]},{"page":8,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"VOTE NO on the City's ask for a $7 million annua general-purpos tax with no","x":298,"y":349,"w":1628,"h":50},{"text":"expiration date.","x":299,"y":409,"w":324,"h":43},{"text":"Tell City Hall: Do better with the tax dollars we already provide.","x":298,"y":498,"w":1307,"h":48},{"text":"Voters remember being told Measure T nd rampant new housing development would \"NOT","x":297,"y":586,"w":1789,"h":51},{"text":"INCREASE TAXES.\"","x":298,"y":646,"w":414,"h":35},{"text":"Promise made.","x":298,"y":734,"w":291,"h":37},{"text":"Now City Hall wants another $7 million annually with no expiration date.","x":298,"y":823,"w":1452,"h":50},{"text":"And for what exactly?","x":294,"y":912,"w":455,"h":46},{"text":"16","x":2144,"y":342,"w":64,"h":56},{"text":"Meuugyoes not exactly specify nor restrict how the $7 mittion must be spent. Its revenue (O","x":296,"y":1001,"w":1916,"h":61},{"text":"is not legally restricted to police, fire, streets, parks, homelessness, or other services.","x":295,"y":1061,"w":1679,"h":47},{"text":"Truthfully, this is a general-purpose x that City Hall can freely use as it pleases,","x":293,"y":1149,"w":1589,"h":51},{"text":"eyeo)nanages a $356 million annual City budget with a projected $16.8 million","x":276,"y":1237,"w":1715,"h":61},{"text":"General Fund deficit.","x":293,"y":1297,"w":434,"h":37},{"text":"Th ity Manager cently received a salary increase to $380,120t before adding employer-","x":290,"y":1386,"w":1776,"h":52},{"text":"paid €fi€fiféGt cost taxpayers even more annually.","x":292,"y":1434,"w":1029,"h":58},{"text":"Voters expect City management to balance the budget, prioritize essential services,","x":290,"y":1533,"w":1684,"h":50},{"text":"improve productivity, and cut wasteful spending before asking residents to pay more.","x":291,"y":1592,"w":1776,"h":53},{"text":"CUT BUDGET WASTE instead of threatening essential-service reductions to persuade","x":291,"y":1681,"w":1781,"h":51},{"text":"voters to approve another tax.","x":290,"y":1743,"w":627,"h":42},{"text":"Before raising taxes, City Hall should scrutinize management and staffing costs, vacancies,","x":291,"y":1829,"w":1787,"h":51},{"text":"consultants and contracts, administrative overhead, operating efficiencies, program priorities,","x":290,"y":1889,"w":1791,"h":50},{"text":"and economic development.","x":290,"y":1947,"w":544,"h":45},{"text":"Please roll up your sleeves and aggressively pursue the millions in Vehicle License Fee (VLF)","x":291,"y":2036,"w":1806,"h":52},{"text":"revenue withheld by the State.","x":291,"y":2096,"w":584,"h":45},{"text":"Taxpayers are the shareholders of City government.","x":668,"y":2186,"w":1076,"h":47},{"text":"We deserve accountability, measurable results, and a complete budget solution—","x":355,"y":2274,"w":1699,"h":49},{"text":"NOT ANOTHER PEN-ENDED AX. VOTE NO.","x":727,"y":2364,"w":962,"h":39},{"text":"www.tasoforsanmateo.com/letsdobetter","x":822,"y":2453,"w":769,"h":39},{"text":"3","x":2169,"y":1306,"w":36,"h":59},{"text":"IO","x":2132,"y":2268,"w":59,"h":49}]}]}
